        "original_id": "8958730e-23b7-5496-a7f1-efde260f22aa",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Cira Centre South, University City, Philadelphia, Pennsylvania, Schuylkill River, Center City Philadelphia\n- Buildings: two skyscrapers, 30th Street Station, Old Post Office Building\n- Organizations: Southeastern Pennsylvania Transportation Authority (SEPTA)\n- Concepts: Center City fare zone\n\nFacts:\n- Cira Centre South is a complex of two skyscrapers in the University City district of Philadelphia, Pennsylvania.\n- Cira Centre South is across the Schuylkill River from Center City Philadelphia.\n- Cira Centre South is located between Walnut Street and Chestnut Street, south of 30th Street Station and the Old Post Office Building.\n- 30th Street Station is the main railroad station in Philadelphia, Pennsylvania, United States.\n- 30th Street Station is one of the seven stations in Southeastern Pennsylvania Transportation Authority's Center City fare zone.",
